/target
**/*.rs.bk
__pycache__/

# .github/fixtures/disallowed-pipes is a standalone crate (its own Cargo.toml), built fresh by
# .github/scripts/check-disallowed-pipes.sh — no reason to pin or track its throwaway lockfile.
/.github/fixtures/disallowed-pipes/Cargo.lock
/.github/fixtures/disallowed-pipes/target

# Claude Code
.claude/*.local.*
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/worktrees/

# Agent scratch: plans, specs, task briefs and reports.
.tmp/
.superpowers/

# Vagrant's own per-machine state (box config, provider config, SSH/WinRM keys). devvm.py
# itself never creates a `.vagrant/` here - it points VAGRANT_DOTFILE_PATH at
# .tmp/devvm/<guest>/.vagrant instead (already covered by the `.tmp/` rule above), so every
# guest's real state is throwaway and regenerated by every `devvm.py up`. This entry only
# guards against `vagrant` being run directly inside scripts/devvm/guests/<name> (bypassing
# devvm.py and its VAGRANT_DOTFILE_PATH redirect), which would otherwise leave Vagrant's
# default per-machine state directory tracked in the repo.
.vagrant/
